# FastAPI security

- Use Pydantic models for every request body/query; reject unknown fields where appropriate.
- Hash passwords with Argon2 or bcrypt (passlib/argon2-cffi). Never store plaintext.
- JWT: short-lived access tokens; prefer httpOnly Secure SameSite cookies over localStorage; rotate refresh tokens.
- Enforce role checks (`organizer` vs `participant`) on every mutating route — never trust client-sent roles.
- Registration/quiz answers: verify event ownership / registration ownership server-side.
- Quiz timing: enforce deadlines and per-question timeouts on the server; ignore client clocks.
- Hide correct answers from participant responses until after submit/event rules allow.
- Enable CORS only for known frontend origins — never `allow_origins=["*"]` with credentials.
- Add rate limiting on auth, register, AI generate, and answer-submit routes.
- Use HTTPS-only in production; set secure cookie flags.
- Dependency-inject DB/auth; avoid global mutable secrets.
- Code must pass Bandit/pip-audit mindset — no `assert` for security checks, no `shell=True`, no hardcoded credentials.

```python
# ❌ BAD — client clock / trusting body for authz
if body.is_organizer:
    return answers

# ✅ GOOD — server-side ownership check
event = await get_event(event_id)
if event.org_id not in current_user.org_ids:
    raise HTTPException(status_code=403, detail="Forbidden")
```
